    <section class="hero" id="home">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow">Voice-first knowledge home</div>
        <h1>EEON</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          A draft landing page direction for a product where notes, decisions, and knowledge stay
          reachable from anywhere, with capture anchored in the thumb zone.
        </p>
        <div class="actions" aria-label="Prototype actions">
          <span class="action-pair">
            <button class="button" type="button" disabled>Capture a note</button>
            <span class="draft-label">Unavailable in draft</span>
          </span>
          <a class="button-link secondary" href="#knowledge">Browse knowledge</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="working-surface" aria-labelledby="surface-heading">
        <div class="surface-title">
          <h2 id="surface-heading">Working Surface</h2>
          <span>Based only on included notes</span>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <div class="row-label">Top Layer</div>
          <div>
            <strong>Knowledge and notes remain anchored at the top.</strong>
            <p>Recorded as an idea, not a shipped layout.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <div class="row-label">Middle</div>
          <div>
            <strong>Persona-shaped areas reorder by signal density.</strong>
            <p>Unresolved: what signals drive this ordering and how users override it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <div class="row-label">Bottom</div>
          <div>
            <strong>Capture stays reachable in the bottom thumb zone.</strong>
            <p class="status">Recorded as a must-have design constraint.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="knowledge">
      <h2>Knowledge Layer</h2>
      <div class="wide-row">
        <h3>Recorded Value</h3>
        <p>
          Knowledge is described as the value layer. This draft makes it a first-viewport path
          rather than hiding it behind a marketing explanation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wide-row">
        <h3>Q&amp;A Scope</h3>
        <p>
          Notes mention Q&amp;A across all notes using compiled article summaries for Tier A and
          map-reduce for Tier C only when scope is huge. This is source context, not proof that
          the feature exists.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wide-row">
        <h3>Essential Placeholders</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>[Exact product category and launch audience unknown]</li>
          <li>[Pricing deck content unknown]</li>
          <li>[Actual onboarding copy not included in packet]</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="design">
      <h2>Design Direction</h2>
      <div class="wide-row">
        <h3>Decision</h3>
        <p>
          Use blue as the accent for the icon, not coral. This is the only explicit visual
          decision in the supplied packet.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wide-row">
        <h3>Recorded Completion</h3>
        <p>
          Marco said onboarding copy is done. The copy itself was not included, so this draft does
          not present it as verified or final.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wide-row">
        <h3>Action From Notes</h3>
        <p>
          Send Lena the pricing deck by Friday at 5 PM. This prototype does not send, schedule, or
          price anything.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="open">
      <h2>Open Questions</h2>
      <div class="wide-row">
        <h3>Product Promise</h3>
        <p>
          What should the public landing page claim EEON does today, versus what is still a product
          direction?
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wide-row">
        <h3>Pricing</h3>
        <p>
          The pricing deck is referenced but not included. Pricing remains an explicit placeholder.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wide-row">
        <h3>Agent Access</h3>
        <p>
          The brief says EEON agent access was not connected when prepared, so this page does not
          assume access to notes beyond the included excerpts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="foot">
      Source note IDs: B77B8019-1129-4B4B-917E-53D30872C5BB,
